==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|de|falb}} {{q|of horses; otherwise archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|val}} (inflected {{m|gmh|valwe}}), from {{inh|de|goh|falo}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*falwaz}}. While the variant {{m|gmh|falb}} is from the Middle High German inflected stem, the form {{m|de||fahl}} is based on the uninflected stem. However, the lengthened vowel points to influence by varieties that reduce ''-lw-'' to ''-l-'' even in open syllables; these include {{der|de|gml|vāl}} (declined {{m|gml|vāle}}), from {{der|de|osx|falu}}. See the same development in {{m|de|kahl}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|vaal}}, {{m+|en|fallow}}.

